    "created_at": "2020-06-07T19:52:05Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-06-07T19:52:25Z",
    "body": "It's not just shaping that breaks, this could also break things like bidi mirroring (well, arguable that's a form of shaping, perhaps). Consider https://codepen.io/jfkthame/pen/zYrGbPo for example: applying `unicode-bidi: isolate` to the `<ins>` and `<del>` elements causes them to render the wrong glyphs.\r\n\r\nA better solution for the reported chromium issue would be to use ::before and ::after to insert ZWNJ each side of the `<ins>` or `<del>` element, if it is important to maintain separate coloring (though this would still break shaping in Ebrahim's example). I don't think this should be part of the default UA stylesheet, but a site that cares more about per-character color than about shaping might choose to do it.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/640270608/reactions",
